 on Udugampola \u2013 Divulapitiya road approximately 2\u00a0km (1.2\u00a0mi) away from Udugampola town. The temple has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka. The designation was declared on 22 November 2002 under the government Gazette number 1264.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Panasawanarama Purana Vihara</b> is a Buddhist temple in Kospillewa, Sri Lanka. The temple is located on Udugampola \u2013 Divulapitiya road approximately 2\u00a0km (1.2\u00a0mi) away from Udugampola town. The temple has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka. The designation was declared on 22 November 2002 under the government Gazette number 1264.</p>"}